  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Low-Head Hydropower Project Portfolio, through Government of Chile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $721,657 feasibility study entails the selection of two low-head hydro projects (Pilot Projects) from a total of four potential sites based on economics and implementation timeframe. The study will conduct assessments and include the engineering designs of the two selected Pilot Projects, as well as identify a portfolio of 50-150 megawatts (Portfolio) of additional low-head hydropower projects and evaluate their viability. The grantee is Telecommunicaciones y Energia, Wireless Energy (Chile) Ltda. (Wireless Energy), an experienced alternative energy project developer based in Puerto Montt in southern Chile. U.S. company Natel Energy, Inc. (Alameda, CA) is the sole-source contractor for this activity. Natel Energy is a U.S. manufacturer that has developed and patented a turbine (hydroEngine TM) for low-head sites that would be used in the hydro plants to be developed by Wireless Energy.</narrative>
  </description>
